.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-DELETE-USER 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-delete-user \- delete a Euclid user account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam delete-user
.BR \-\-userId | \-u
.I USERID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes the user identified by \fIUSERID\fR via the eam service's
.I delete-user
action. The caller must be authenticated as an administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)).
.PP
On success, a confirmation message naming the deleted user ID is printed
to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-userId " " \fIUSERID\fR
User ID of the account to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The user was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller is
not an authenticated administrator, or no user with that ID exists. If
the failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the
stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam delete-user --userId jdoe
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-users (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
